(text "CoCo 3 2 MB SRAM expansion - memory board (plugs into CN4/CN5/CN6)" (at 25.40 30.48 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid fd6b30d4-5186-41c4-9f19-9a5cbd69cfd4))
(text "Remove IC16-IC19 and cut C65, C66 first (as for any 512K upgrade)." (at 25.40 35.56 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid fc7f3017-6374-4574-821c-7a4edbbec366))
(text "J3 (G G B0 B1) takes BANK0/BANK1 (physical A19/A20) from the DAT board. Unconnected: R1/R2 pull low = 512K mode." (at 25.40 40.64 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 0617a619-05a5-493d-a44d-7d3c7c15a1af))
(text "Write logic (active low): ~BHE = ~WE0 XOR 1   ~BLE = ~WE1 XOR 1   ~WE = ~WE1 XOR ~BHE" (at 160.02 30.48 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 6ce9a95f-b5da-4a31-a74c-d384fee956b1))
(text "RAS = ~RAS XOR 1 clocks U3/U4: row address (9 bits) and BANK1:0 latched on the falling edge of ~RAS." (at 160.02 35.56 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 926df40a-0716-4552-813a-acf398f38bf8))
(text "SRAM ~CE1 = ~CAS, CE2 = BYTE = 1 (x16), ~OE = 0. Address/data pin order is permuted for routing." (at 160.02 40.64 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 05eb6032-e387-4bc2-b979-c2111445fa8b))
(text "Derived from cc3-512k by Ciaran Anscomb (CC BY-SA 4.0), logic per Jim Brain. This design is CC BY-SA 4.0." (at 25.40 256.54 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid dbf0ecb3-d5fd-44c6-98df-fc57cc69a4a2))
